  "result": {
    "decision": "measurement_repair_core_stack_does_not_lose_in_chop",
    "diagnostic_only": true,
    "accepted": false,
    "summary": "The core accepted stack does NOT lose in chop: chop-bucket mean PnL is +$2,991 (positive) and Spearman(p_choppy, pnl) is +0.116 pooled and positive in all three windows -- the opposite sign of the FGRS sleeve (-0.324). The core enters in chop only 10% of the time because its entry gates already concentrate entries in trend regimes. Applying the regime_chop_state soft down-tilt to the whole core book would have cut core PnL by -$29,048 (~12%). Conclusion: chop-sensitivity is sleeve-specific, not portfolio-wide. A portfolio-level chop tilt must be scoped to the default-off sleeves with individually-negative Spearman(p_choppy, pnl), never the core stack, and validated on forward entry-regime-tagged rows -- not by re-slicing these frozen windows. Caveat: chop-bucket N is small (6 core trades); direction is robust across windows, magnitude is indicative.",
